{"files":[{"content":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\nstatic inline uint32x4_t add_mod(uint32x4_t a, uint32x4_t b) {\n    const uint32x4_t modulus = vdupq_n_u32(MOD);\n    const uint32x4_t sum = vaddq_u32(a, b);\n    return vsubq_u32(sum, vandq_u32(vcgeq_u32(sum, modulus), modulus));\n}\n#endif\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    vector<vector<bool> > blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n, false));\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int i, j;\n        cin >> i >> j;\n        blockedCells[i][j] = true;\n    }\n\n    vector<unsigned int> dp(n, 0);\n    dp[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        unsigned int carry = 0;\n        int j = 0;\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n        const uint32x4_t zero = vdupq_n_u32(0);\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            if (!(blockedCells[i][j] || blockedCells[i][j + 1] ||\n                  blockedCells[i][j + 2] || blockedCells[i][j + 3])) {\n                uint32x4_t values = vld1q_u32(dp.data() + j);\n                values = add_mod(values, vextq_u32(zero, values, 3));\n                values = add_mod(values, vextq_u32(zero, values, 2));\n                values = add_mod(values, vdupq_n_u32(carry));\n                vst1q_u32(dp.data() + j, values);\n                carry = vgetq_lane_u32(values, 3);\n            } else {\n                for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k) {\n                    unsigned int value = dp[j + k] + carry;\n                    if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n                    if (blockedCells[i][j + k]) value = 0;\n                    dp[j + k] = carry = value;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n#endif\n        for (; j < n; ++j) {\n            unsigned int value = dp[j] + carry;\n            if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n            if (blockedCells[i][j]) value = 0;\n            dp[j] = carry = value;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << endl;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"A four-lane NEON modular prefix scan can accelerate obstacle-free blocks without violating the horizontal dependency; in-place row updates also eliminate row copying.","notes":"Blocked blocks and tails use the exact scalar recurrence. Each modular addition stays below twice MOD. Includes a non-AArch64 scalar fallback; no performance or correctness evaluation was executed.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace two DP rows and row copying with one in-place row and an explicit left carry.","Use an inclusive four-lane NEON prefix scan for blocks without obstacles, adding the incoming carry after the scan.","Replace integer remainder with bounded conditional subtraction; retain scalar processing for blocked blocks and tails."]}